      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 42,
      "reasoning": "This is an Objective criterion because it requires specific posterior summary statistics for M33 X-7. The report uses the full joint posterior and gives quantitatively consistent medians and 68% intervals, but it does not explicitly report the required marginalized means and standard deviations, so direct verification against the paper is incomplete."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 28,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. The report does compute a smooth Monte Carlo posterior-integrated M33 X-7 curve over the appropriate boson-mass scale and includes an equivalent 95% threshold, but it plots the complementary exclusion probability, uses a substantially different fiducial lifetime (45 Myr versus the target’s 3 Myr), and does not reproduce the target’s distinct n=2, n≤6, uncorrected, and box curves. Consequently, the exclusion interval and high-mass structure are not directly comparable to the published target and show significant methodological/visual deviations."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "text",
      "weight": 0.5,
      "score": 25,
      "reasoning": "This is an Objective (Mode A) criterion. The report presents 95% self-interaction constraints for M33 X-7 over specified boson masses, but reports them in terms of $f_a$ and $|\\lambda|$, not the required upper limit on $g$ in GeV$^{-1}$; moreover, its bosenova treatment is explicitly order-of-magnitude and the claimed confidence construction is not a rigorous credible upper limit on $g$."
     }
    ],
